final_image_tex = SubResource("Resource_5a5dv")
blurb = "Depicts a scholar's shelf-desk with writing materials and a potted plant in from of a screen painted with a wave.

The print features embossing and metallic pigment to create sparkling grooves in the desk.

Two verses are inscribed on the print. The one on the left is by Kyōkadō Magao (1753–1829):

[i]In the capital where sweet potatoes bake in pots, I would not trade them for the mountain yams of the jeweled-spear Michinoku.[/i]

The comical poem expresses local pride in the sweet potatoes of Edo (a cheap street food). The \"jeweled spear\" (\"tamaboko\") is a traditional prefix for the word michi (\"road\"), here used as a pun to introduce Michinoku, the name of a region corresponding to modern-day northeastern Tōhoku.

The verse on the right I could not translate or attribute with a sufficient level of confidence to present here. It is signed 花栖亭 真芳."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://6kpsqyb2pk7a"
